<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:37Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Tunisia: Judge orders arrest of journalist Mohamed Yousfi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:865c6ae1af87f75f769288831a28cbf578f47ac4d5555aee77aebb05a559f89a</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T03:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tunisia-judge-orders-arrest-of-journalist-mohamed-yousfi/a-79040802--a89422e15909.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tunisia-judge-orders-arrest-of-journalist-mohamed-yousfi/a-79040802?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A journalist and vocal critic of the Tunisian president, Mohamed Yousfi has been taken into custody ahead of an interview. A union called the arrest an attack on all journalists' rights.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UN approves world map reflecting true size of Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d28a5c7eb3f50dcf135a0c42a7432f2fc524dff3682508c265030567b9679494</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T23:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/un-approves-world-map-reflecting-true-size-of-africa/a-79040629--e6486bc869d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/un-approves-world-map-reflecting-true-size-of-africa/a-79040629?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The UN General Assembly voted to adopt a map that more accurately shows the size of the continents. Only the United States voted against the measure, which projects the country as smaller than on traditional maps.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria: Suspected oil thieves dead after inhaling fumes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3617e45a9cf0b57fa1d78b5bc610138ab630955d0e487df7b442b084ec62718a</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-suspected-oil-thieves-dead-after-inhaling-fumes/a-79001997--76c34d7b815f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-suspected-oil-thieves-dead-after-inhaling-fumes/a-79001997?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Nigerian environmental group says that at least 37 people died trying to siphon crude oil off a ship illegally. Police acknowledged a fatal incident but gave fewer details, saying investigations continued.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How can African retailers compete with Shein and Temu?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79945ed808f8eb2e68ab7f3b26be2545819d98613bb395db3e819616d09a408a</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-can-african-retailers-compete-with-shein-and-temu/a-78988195--3bda9e77e49f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-can-african-retailers-compete-with-shein-and-temu/a-78988195?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Shein and Temu are expanding across Africa with low prices and vast product ranges. Businesses and unions warn the growth could come at a cost for local jobs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Tunisia's activists decry civil society crackdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45b2aa639ae75339b259812c6a3d61b0271114ccefb8a98c03c0366d76e07db4</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T04:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tunisia-s-activists-decry-civil-society-crackdown/a-78614966--e657463dce69.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tunisia-s-activists-decry-civil-society-crackdown/a-78614966?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Five years into Tunisian President Kais Saied’s increasingly authoritarian rule, rights groups warn that the country’s once vibrant civil society is being silenced.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Congo's Ebola caseload tops 6,000 as concerns grow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b159f65ace57a8ff417fe8c57819bf0501cd173a945fc4562a47e786ceeb4de0</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T18:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-caseload-tops-6-000-as-concerns-grow/a-78638447--5f990f71c7d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-caseload-tops-6-000-as-concerns-grow/a-78638447?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo has surpassed 6,000 confirmed cases, with nearly 3,000 deaths. As the virus spreads, authorities are racing to contain one of the deadliest outbreaks in history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
